The file plumb is about to overwrite (the prior generated output, identified by
the -output base name) must not contribute providers, so a stray directive left
in it is never fed back as input. Here plumb_gen.go is the output base and holds a
ghost provider of *Config; it is skipped, so generation succeeds and never names
ghost. (Its control is overwrite_stale_scanned_no_output.txtar: the same files
with no identified output base, where ghost IS scanned and collides.)
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app
type Config struct{}
type Server struct{}
//plumb:build
func NewConfig() *Config { return &Config{} }
//plumb:build
func NewServer(c *Config) *Server { return &Server{} }
-- example.com/app/plumb_gen.go --
package app
//plumb:build
func ghost() *Config { return nil }
